  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In 2023, Hung Cao posted on X that having China work in AI for U.S. defense was “like asking the fox to guard the henhouse.” As Acting Secretary of the Navy in 2026, Cao said a data and AI strategy would help build an “AI-first” Fleet and turn information into warfighting advantage. He also said the Navy needs AI to get “faster, better, smarter,” and a reported strategy described establishing an AI War Council. Cao described drones and cruise missiles as arriving within seconds.",
   "sids": [
